Ladybird ignores connection-specific fields in an HTTP/2 response and
keeps the response. It still checks a request’s fields as nghttp2 does.

Gecko drops the same fields from a response (connection, keep-alive,
proxy-connection, te, transfer-encoding and upgrade) in the method
Http2Decompressor::OutputHeader(), and delivers the rest. Chromium’s
SpdyHeadersToHttpResponse() accepts the response with those fields, and
only CreateSpdyHeadersFromHttpRequest() leaves them out of a request.
